{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.trivial_model","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.trivial_model","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L115-L120","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** The one-channel degenerate model (`e_plus = 1`, `e_minus = 0`, `σ = q`)\ninhabits the class for any invertible `q`, so the axiomatisation is consistent. The\nfaithful two-channel model lives in the commutant of `σ₁` in `H_2(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.channel_algebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.channel_algebra","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L102-L113","doc":"**The bundled channel-algebra proposition** — the Lean face of\n`prop:two-vortex-channel-algebra`: from the four channel hypotheses (partition,\northogonality, inverse witness, spectral form), *all* ring-level conclusions follow —\nderived idempotency of both channels, the spectral square, and the Hecke relation.\n(The eigenvalue-ratio identity is the companion lemma `eigenvalue_ratio` above, kept\nseparate because it needs only the inverse witness, no channel data.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:two-vortex-channel-algebra","label":"prop:two-vortex-channel-algebra","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/two-vortex-channel-algebra.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.eigenvalue_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.eigenvalue_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L88-L100","doc":"**Per-crossing suppression ratio.** The ratio of the antisymmetric to the symmetric\nchannel eigenvalue is `(−q⁻¹)/q = −(q²)⁻¹`: each crossing damps the antisymmetric\ndisturbance by `q⁻²` relative to the symmetric carrier.\n\nStated **division-free** (§7c, the R[h] pattern) in the file's own idiom, with `u` the\nring-level witness of `q⁻¹`: the ratio `r = −u²` is characterised by `r · q = −u`,\nwhich is the cleared form of `(−q⁻¹)/q = −(q²)⁻¹`. No field is needed — `q · u = 1` is\nthe only input, so the statement lives over the same `CommRing` as the rest of the file\nrather than importing a `Field` (and its `0⁻¹ = 0` junk convention) for one lemma.\nThat the ratio is a *decay* — `q⁻² < 1` — is the archimedean statement `q > 1`, made\nonly past the wall, §7c. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.hecke_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.hecke_relation","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L77-L86","doc":"**The channel model satisfies the Hecke relation** `σ² = (q − u)·σ + 1` — the\nabstract two-channel data reproduces the skein/Hecke relation of AGENTS.md §7a with the\ninverse witness `u` in the `q⁻¹` slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.braiding_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.braiding_sq","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L66-L75","doc":"**The Hopf-link interaction, spectrally.** The square of the braiding (two crossings\n— the closure is the Hopf link) decomposes as `σ² = q²·e_plus + u²·e_minus`: the symmetric\nchannel is weighted `q²`, the antisymmetric channel `u² = q⁻²`. Needs only partition +\northogonality, not invertibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.idem_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.idem_minus","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L62-L64","doc":"**Idempotency of the antisymmetric channel is derived**: `e_minus² = e_minus`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.idem_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.idem_plus","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L57-L60","doc":"**Idempotency of the symmetric channel is derived**, not assumed:\n`e_plus² = e_plus` follows from partition + orthogonality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.eigen","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Spectral form of the braiding: `σ = q·e_plus − u·e_minus` (eigenvalues `q`, `−q⁻¹`;\nAGENTS.md §7a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.inverse","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L50-L50","doc":"`u` witnesses `q⁻¹` at ring level: `q·u = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The channels are orthogonal: `e_plus·e_minus = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.partition","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The two channels partition unity: `e_plus + e_minus = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.TwoVortexChannels","kind":"class","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/TwoVortexChannelAlgebra.lean#L39-L53","doc":"**Two-vortex channel data, as a class.** `σ` is the braiding of the two-vortex\ninteraction; `e₊`/`e₋` the symmetric/antisymmetric channel projectors (partition of\nunity, orthogonal); `q` and `−u` the two channel eigenvalues, with `u` a ring-level\ninverse witness for `q`. The intended model is the commutant of `σ₁` in `H_2(q)` with\n`e₊ = (σ + q⁻¹)/(q + q⁻¹)`, `e₋ = (q − σ)/(q + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}